<title>UK: C&amp;W in talks with U.S. firms - paper.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W in talks with U.S. firms - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cable and Wireless chief executive Dick Brown is in talks with AT &amp; T and Sprint Corp about forming a 20 billion pound ($32 billion) global alliance, the Sunday Times newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The paper said Brown had confirmed talks were being held in anticipation of the ending of C&amp;W's link-up with its German partner Veba, announced on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be completely free and it's up to us to decide who we want as a global partner, if anybody. We are an enormously attractive partner,&quot; the paper quoted Brown as saying.</p>
</text>
